{
  "category": "wrong_dangerous",
  "names_missing_fact": false,
  "rationale": "The answer correctly rejects the idea that the car cannot be sold, but it materially misstates California law by saying the vehicle exemption is not automatic at all and is waived if no claim is filed. The ground truth says the first $7,500 of sale proceeds is automatically paid to the debtor even without a claim, and the claim-of-exemption deadline is 15 days from personal service, September 25, 2026. The answer gives an earlier 10-day/September 21 deadline and understates the debtor’s automatic protection, which could mislead the consumer to her detriment."
}
